NAME
       cksum - print a CRC checksum and byte count of files

SYNOPSIS
       cksum [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
       For each FILE (or standard input), cksum prints a 32-bit CRC checksum,
       the number of bytes, and the name. It is a quick check that two copies
       are the same; for anything that matters, use sha256sum, which is much
       harder to fool.

EXAMPLES
           cksum /etc/hosts /tmp/hosts.copy

SEE ALSO
       sha256sum(1), md5sum(1), b2sum(1), cmp(1)
